    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "SWITCHES\n\nA Switch routes execution by VALUE instead of by true/false.\n  Switch On Int: Case0..Case3, Default     Switch On String: Option1..Option3, Default\n  Range Switch: Negative (<0), Low (<10), Medium (<50), High (<100), Extreme (the rest)\n  String Contains Switch: the first pattern found in the text, or None.\nA Sequence node runs its Then pins in order, so all four demos run one after another.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          230.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "SEQUENCE\nRuns Then0, Then1, Then2, Then3 in that order. Each Then starts a separate chain.",
        "position": [
          360.0,
          130.0
        ],
        "size": [
          270.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.55,
          0.55,
          0.6,
          0.28
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "seq"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "INT SWITCH\nvalue = 2 takes Case2. Any value above 3 (or below 0) would take Default. Outputs you do not wire simply do nothing.",
        "position": [
          660.0,
          -110.0
        ],
        "size": [
          640.0,
          110.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
